-- Ekwo OS — Seychelles: chart of accounts, journals, taxes and defaults.
--
-- Generated from packs/sc at version 0.1.0, do not edit.
-- Change the pack and run `ekwo pack build sc`; `ekwo pack check --all`
-- refuses a seed that is not the exact output of its pack, and the CI runs it.
--
-- Community pack — not reviewed.
-- Written from:
--   Value Added Tax (Amendment of Schedules) Regulations, 2014 (S.I. 4 of 2014, made under section 52(1) of the Value Added Tax Act, Act 35 of 2010) — repeals and replaces the Schedules: First Schedule Part II (exempt supplies, items 1 to 5), Second Schedule (zero-rated supplies), Third Schedule (rate of VAT, 15 %), Fourth Schedule (registration threshold, SCR 3,000,000 in this text) (Minister of Finance, Trade and Investment (Supplement to the Official Gazette, 20 January 2014; copy hosted by the World Trade Organization))
--     https://www.wto.org/english/thewto_e/acc_e/syc_e/wtaccsyc48_leg_2.pdf
--   Seychelles Revenue Commission — Value Added Tax Return: lines 1 to 11, columns A (value) and B (VAT), with the instructions for completing it; the return is lodged with the Business Activity Statement by the 21st of the month following the taxable period (Seychelles Revenue Commission (SRC))
--     https://www.src.gov.sc/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/VATReturn-manual.pdf
--   Revenue Law (Amendment) Act 2023 (Act 27 of 2023, Supplement to the Official Gazette, 22 December 2023) — new section 3(1) and (2) of the Revenue Administration Act: a monthly return is furnished by the 21st day of the month when furnished in person and by the 23rd when furnished through the SRC Tax Portal, and a large business furnishes through the Portal; new section 20: the monthly tax is paid by the 21st in person and by the 23rd through the Portal or by bank transfer, and a payment of SCR 50,000 or more goes through the Portal (National Assembly of Seychelles)
--     https://src.gov.sc/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Act-27-2023-Revenue-Law-Amendment-Act-2023.pdf
--   What is Value Added Tax (VAT)? — information brochure: standard rate 15 %, zero-rated supplies (mainly exports) as taxable supplies at 0 % with input tax deductible, exempt supplies with no right to deduct (Seychelles Revenue Commission (SRC))
--     https://www.src.gov.sc/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/VAT-Guideline.pdf
--   SRC guidance on the amendments made to the Fourth Schedule of the VAT Act 2010 (S.I. 97 of 2024): compulsory registration at SCR 2,000,000 of taxable supplies, voluntary registration from SCR 100,000, application within 14 days (Seychelles Revenue Commission (SRC))
--     https://src.gov.sc/src-provides-guidance-on-amendments-made-to-the-fourth-schedule-of-vat-act-2010/
--   Business Activity Statement — the form on which the VAT due (box 10A of the return) is paid, with the other monthly taxes; due by the 21st day of the month following (Seychelles Revenue Commission (SRC))
--     https://src.gov.sc/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Business-Activity-Statement-Form.pdf
--   IAS 1 Presentation of Financial Statements — the statement of financial position and the statement of profit or loss, expenses analysed by nature; no Seychelles text prescribing a layout or a chart of accounts was found (IFRS Foundation)
--     https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/list-of-standards/ias-1-presentation-of-financial-statements/
--   Seychelles Revenue Commission — tax administration portal (forms, guidance, Tax Portal for returns and payments) (Seychelles Revenue Commission (SRC))
--     https://www.src.gov.sc
--
-- Reference data: `install_country_template()` copies it into a company,
-- nothing here belongs to a company.

